# Pyking mixes no numbers on its own.
#
# `+ - * /` and the comparisons each take two operands of one type, so
# an Int beside a Float is refused rather than widened. Implicit
# widening would mean the operands were no longer unified before the
# operator table was asked, which is the assumption the whole table
# rests on -- and it would make `1 / 2` change meaning with context.
# The refusal names the way out.

print(1 + 1.0)
